ReadMe file for MineHunt

INTRODUCTION

MineHunt is a simple game for the Psion 3 and Acorn Pocketbook. It is 
distributed on 3.5 inch disk in either PC or Archimedes format for 
downloading with either the PC 3 Link or Acorn A Link.  

MineHunt is written in OPL and installs as an OPA. It can be installed 
in the main memory or from a flash EPROM or RAM card.

PC 

Use the 3 Link to copy the minopa.opa card to the APP directory on the 
appropriate device (M,A or B). Then go to the install application menu 
on the Psion 3, this will show the minopa application as being 
available to install. Install it and start it like any other OPA. 


ARCHIMEDES

To install from the Archimedes the aim is to copy the minopa file to 
the APP directory on the M,A or B device on the Psion/Pocketbook and 
then rename the file to minopa.opa.

Use the A link software to show the root directory on the pocket book 
device and then select the APP directory (if there isn't such a 
directory you may have to create one). 

Copy the file using drop and drag (as normal on the ARC).  Then move to 
the Psion/Pocket Book and rename the file, (it will probably have 
copied as  APPminopa.ris and needs to be APPminopa.opa ).

Then go to the install application menu on the Psion 3, this will show 
the minopa application as being available to install. Install it and 
start it like any other OPA. 

THE GAME

The aim of MineHunt is to identify the squares which contain mines by 
marking squares as either Clear or as containing a Mine. Marking a 
square which contains a mine as Clear will explode the mine and lose 
the game.

The main menu offers options of Play,Options,Help,Info,Quit

PLAY

When Play is selected the minefield is initialised (which may take some 
seconds) and then drawn. The minefield displays as a grid with one 
square inverted. This is the currently selected square.

The arrow keys change the currently selected square, moving in the 
direction of the arrow. 

The 'C' key designates a square as clear. If the square has mines in 
neighbouring squares  the count of the number of neighboring mines will 
be displayed . Pressing 'C' over a square which contains a mine will 
explode the mine and end the current game. Pressing 'C' over a square 
with no neighbours displays that square as blank and acts as if the 'C' 
key had been pressed on all neighbouring squares, the effect of this 
can be to reveal the status of a large area of the board.

The 'M' key designates a square as containing a mine. This need not be 
final and if you decide a mistake has been made pressing 'M' over the 
square again will undo the selection.

During play the ESC key can be used to quit the current game and return 
to the main menu. This counts as losing the current game! Confirmation 
is requested before quitting.

OPTIONS

The Options selection from the main menu allows either 15,30 or 45 
mines to be selected. The default of 15 is a good level for beginners, 
30 is difficult, and 45 is almost impossible!

HELP and INFO

The Help and Info selections offer simple Help and Versions screens.

QUIT
The Quit selection exits the MineHunt Program. The icon will remain on 
the menu bar. Quitting causes the score table to be reset.

Happy MineHunting!
